Spec: Follow route

Purpose:
  Riding a saved route again, with or without recording, and linking a recorded follow to its original.

Owns:
  ./*.dart
  ./widgets/*.dart
  /test/follow

References:
  /docs/specs/history/17-follow-route.md
  /docs/specs/history/18-follow-reverse.md
  /docs/specs/history/20-followed-rides.md
  /lib/domain/follow_tracker.sdd

Must:
  @routeFollowProvider is process-lifetime and `null` means no reference; then every screen behaves
    as without the feature.
  Follow route is offered for rides with a route from the detail dialog and first in the card menu; a route
    with fewer than two points or no length explains why it cannot be followed.
  The rider chooses Record (countdown and ride screen) or Just follow (`/follow`, foreground only).
  Recording follows read the recorder's position; follow-only runs its own GPS feed while the screen is in
    the foreground.
  Fixes worse than `30` m and seeds older than `2` min are ignored.
  The reference clears on Home's normal start, on leaving the ride screen and on End.
  End and back ask first on the follow screen; before joining it offers Navigate to start.
  The flip button shows once joined; an automatic reverse explains itself once in a snack bar.
  A recorded follow that joined the route is linked to its original when recording stops, with coverage
    and time on the route; following a follow follows its original.

Must not:
  Change @RideTracker or the recorded track.
